msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:145
msgid "View requests"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:154
msgid "General"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:157
msgid "Withdrawal period (days)"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:159
msgid "Statutory minimum is 14 days from delivery. The window starts when the order is marked completed, or at order creation if it never was."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:165
msgid "Form page"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:168
msgid "Withdrawal form page"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:174
msgid "Select a page"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:177
msgid "Create a page with the [withdraw_form] shortcode, then select it here so the My Account button can link to it."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:186
msgid "Eligibility"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:187
msgid "Customers can only submit a withdrawal for orders in one of these statuses. If none are checked, Completed and Processing are used."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:200
msgid "No status checked: Completed and Processing will be saved instead."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:205
msgid "Where the function appears"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:210
msgid "Show a withdrawal link in the site footer"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:212
msgid "The order view only reaches a signed-in customer looking at that order. Article 11a asks for the function to be easily accessible for the whole withdrawal period, so a footer link, a menu item or the [withdraw_link] shortcode on a legal page covers the shoppers the order view does not."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:215
msgid "Link text"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:216
#: src/Frontend/MyAccount.php:50
#: src/Frontend/WithdrawLink.php:65
msgid "Withdraw from contract here"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:217
msgid "Leave empty for the statutory wording. Article 11a(1) prescribes \"withdraw from contract here\" or an unambiguous equivalent, so if you change it, keep it unambiguous."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:223
msgid "Guest access"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:228
msgid "Email a one-time link instead of opening the form straight away"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:230
msgid "Off by default: a customer opens the form with their order number and billing email. Turn this on and the form emails a one-time link to the order billing address instead, so knowing the order number is not enough. Signed-in customers reaching the form from My Account are never asked for a link. This makes the withdrawal function depend on your shop outgoing email working."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:233
msgid "This site is not served over HTTPS. The one-time link travels in a page address and in a form field, so anyone able to watch the connection can read it."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:239
msgid "Digital content"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:244
msgid "Ask for Article 16(m) consent at checkout for downloadable products"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:246
msgid "Adds one optional, unticked checkbox to the checkout when the cart contains a downloadable product. It carries both halves of Article 16(m): the request to start supply immediately and the acknowledgement of losing the right of withdrawal. Once a file has actually been downloaded, that item stops being withdrawable. Virtual products that are not downloadable are services and are not covered."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:249
msgid "The box is never required. A customer who declines keeps the right of withdrawal and still gets the download, because WooCommerce grants download access regardless. That is the law working as intended, not a fault: consent that is a condition of purchase is not freely given, and would not hold up as an exclusion."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:252
msgid "Turning this back off restores the right of withdrawal on past orders too. Granting a withdrawal you could have refused is always lawful; honouring consent from a feature you have switched off would be the surprising outcome."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:258
msgid "Emails"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:261
msgid "Notification email"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:263
msgid "Where new-request notifications are sent. Leave empty to use the site admin email. The customer always gets a confirmation at their own address."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:266
msgid "Every message this plugin sends is a WooCommerce email: same template, same logo, same footer as your order emails, and each one can be reworded or switched off on its own."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:273
msgid "(off)"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:282
msgid "Returns"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:285
msgid "Return address"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:286
msgid "Printed in the message that tells the customer their withdrawal was accepted. Leave empty to use your WooCommerce store address."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:290
msgid "Neither this field nor your WooCommerce store address is filled in, so the acceptance message will not say where to send the goods."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:293
msgid "Who pays to send the goods back"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:295
msgid "Say nothing"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:296
msgid "The customer"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:297
msgid "We do"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:299
msgid "Article 14(1) only lets you charge the customer for the return if you told them so before they bought, in your withdrawal information. If you did not, the cost is yours, which is why this says nothing until you choose."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:302
msgid "Return cost, extra wording"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:303
msgid "Optional, added after the sentence above. Article 6(1)(i) wants an estimate of the cost for goods that cannot normally be sent back by post."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:304
msgid "For example: bulky items are collected by courier, around 40 EUR."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: the sentence the customer will read
#: src/Admin/Settings.php:312
#, php-format
msgid "The customer will read: %s"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:315
msgid "The acceptance message will not mention who pays for the return."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:319
msgid "Your own clock: Article 13(1) gives you 14 days from the day the customer tells you they are withdrawing to refund them, including the standard delivery cost they paid. The request log shows that date and marks it when it passes."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:325
msgid "Legal texts"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:328
msgid "Seller name"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:330
msgid "The trading name that appears in the model withdrawal form and the withdrawal instructions. Empty uses the site title. The address comes from your WooCommerce store address."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:333
msgid "Seller email"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:335
msgid "Seller phone"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:337
msgid "Annex I asks for a telephone number and email address where available, so a consumer can declare by any means."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:340
msgid "Your WooCommerce store address is empty, so the model withdrawal form cannot state a geographical address. Fill it in under WooCommerce, Settings, General."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:343
msgid "Form intro text"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:344
msgid "Shown above the order lookup step. Leave empty for the wording below, which is translated with the rest of the plugin."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:348
msgid "Model withdrawal text"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:349
msgid "Shown on the items step. Leave empty and the plugin generates the statutory model withdrawal form (Annex I.B) from the seller details above, in the language of the site."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:353
msgid "The model instructions on withdrawal (Annex I.A) are pre-contractual information, so they belong on a page of their own rather than on the form. Put the [withdraw_instructions] shortcode on your terms or returns page and the plugin generates them from the same details, including your withdrawal period."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:356
msgid "Digital content consent, extra wording"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:357
msgid "Optional, and added in front of the statutory sentence rather than replacing it. The plugin refuses withdrawal for downloaded items on the strength of the acknowledgement in that sentence, so wording that only promised immediate delivery would take away a right nobody gave up. Whatever the customer sees is stored with their order, so editing this later does not rewrite what earlier customers agreed to."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:358
msgid "For example: these files are available the moment your payment clears."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: the statutory Article 16(m) consent sentence
#: src/Admin/Settings.php:364
#, php-format
msgid "The checkbox always ends with: %s"
msgstr ""

